mia-docs: Heads-up: noticed several teams hit parse regressions when tool outputs use union shapes (string | {text: string}) or nullable fields. We need a short docs section showing canonical patterns + an SDK normalization helper.

noah-ml: Agree. Example failure: schema expects string but some tools return { text: null } or null -> parser accepts but callers blow up. Docs should recommend one of: 1) explicit envelope with discriminator, 2) non-nullable canonical shape, or 3) document null as an explicit signal.

rachel-sdk: I can add a tiny helper in the SDK that normalizes unions into a stable shape. Draft Python snippet for docs:

```python
def normalize_tool_output(payload: dict) -> dict:
    # normalize union: allow str or {text: str} or None -> always {text: str|null}
    if isinstance(payload, str):
        return {"text": payload}
    if payload is None:
        return {"text": None}
    if isinstance(payload, dict) and "text" in payload:
        return {"text": payload.get("text")}
    # fallback: coerce to string
    return {"text": str(payload)}
```

and a short TypeScript equivalent:

```ts
export function normalizeToolOutput(raw: any): { text: string | null } {
  if (typeof raw === 'string') return { text: raw };
  if (raw === null) return { text: null };
  if (typeof raw === 'object' && 'text' in raw) return { text: raw.text ?? null };
  return { text: String(raw) };
}
```

ian-qa: I'll add test vectors to the docs PR: string, object-with-text, null, object-with-null-text, and a weird numeric case. Also include an AJV/JSONSchema example that validates the normalized shape (simple schema for { text: [string,null] }).

noah-ml: Docs should also include guidance: prefer explicit discriminator for richer unions (e.g., {type: 'text', text: '...'}) and avoid ad-hoc nulls unless they carry semantic meaning. Add a migration checklist for teams: bump SDK, run normalizer in ingress, add schema validation, and set telemetry flag "union_normalized" for 1 release.

